2:Tebc,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp#article","headline":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas with MCP","description":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas over MCP and skip the context drift you get from copy-pasting into a chatbot. The Model Context Protocol exposes the Melius canvas as live, structured data an agent can read and act on. Here is how to connect Claude to Melius, what the tools actually are, and why the loop self-corrects.","url":"https://www.melius.com/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp"},"datePublished":"2026-07-20","dateModified":"2026-07-20","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Melius Team","url":"https://www.melius.com"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#organization"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#website"},"inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://www.melius.com/images/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp/cover.webp","timeRequired":"PT6M","wordCount":778,"articleSection":"Melius News","keywords":"Melius News"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Blog","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas with MCP","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Model Context Protocol (MCP)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MCP is an open standard that lets an AI agent connect to a server and call the tools and resources that server exposes. It started with IDEs and terminals, and the same pattern lets an agent read and act on a live creative canvas instead of a screenshot."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Claude MCP?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude MCP just means using the Model Context Protocol with Claude as the host: Claude connects to an MCP server and calls the tools it exposes. Point it at the Melius connector and Claude can read and act on your live canvas directly, rather than working from a pasted description. The protocol is host-agnostic, so any MCP-compatible model works the same way."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I connect Claude to Melius?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The recommended path is the hosted connector. Add a custom MCP connector in your host and point it at https://mcp.melius.com/mcp, then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. Melius mints a durable, revocable connector key for that team, so there is nothing to paste and nothing to refresh."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the agent generate the images and video itself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The host model (for example Claude) is the agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do. The images, video, and audio are produced by the generation models available on the platform, selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a model other than Claude?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any MCP-compatible host. Melius is model-agnostic at the host level."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What stops the agent from acting on nodes that no longer exist?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas, so if it references something that is no longer there, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state."}}]}]}7:X
